.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-GET-BUCKET-ERN 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-get-bucket-ern \- resolve a bucket's ERN by name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm get-bucket-ern
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolves the Euclid resource name (ERN) of a bucket by its name. The
ERN is what most other
.B esm
actions (e.g.
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-bucket (1))
require to identify the bucket.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the bucket to resolve. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The bucket's ERN is printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or no
bucket with that name exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm get-bucket-ern \e
    --name reports
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-create-bucket (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-buckets (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
